Flags 
----

1. IPC_NOWAIT  

	IPC_NOWAIT is a flag used with System V message queue operations (msgsnd(), msgrcv())
	
	Meaning :- 

		* Tells the system call not to block 
		* The call returns immediately if the operation cannot be completed 

	With msgrcv() 

		msgrcv(msgid, &msg, size, type, IPC_NOWAIT);
		
		Behaviour : 

			if a message of the requested type exists -> message is received 
			if no such message exists -> function fails immediately 
		
		Error 

			errno = ENOMSG 
		
		No waiting, No blocking 

	with msgsnd() 
	
		msgsnd(msqid, &msg, size, IPC_NOWAIT);

		Behaviour : 

			if the queue has space -> message is sent
			if the queue is full -> function fails immediately 

		Error 

			errno = EAGAIN

	Why IPC_NOWAIT is Used 

		* To avoid blocking the process 
		* Useful in real-time, embedded, or event-driven programs 
		* Allows program to handle "no message" case manually 
	

2. MSG_EXCEPT 

	MSG_EXCEPT is a flag used with msgrcv() in System V message queues.

	Usage 

		msgrcv(msqid, &msg, size, msgtyp, MSG_EXCEPT);

	Meaning 

		Used only when msgtyp > 0 
		Receives the first message in the queue whose type is not equal to msgtyp 

			Reads the first message except the one with the given msg type

	Behaviour 

		* If msg with a different type exists -> it is received
		* If all messages are of type msgtyp -> the call blocks
			(or fails immediately if IPC_NOWAIT is also used)

	Common use case 

		* skip certain msg types
		* prioritize or filter messages 
		* ignore control or system messages
	
	Example 	

		msgrcv(msqid, &msg, size, 10, MSG_EXCEPT);

		Received the 1st msg whose mtype != 10

3. MSG_NOERROR 
		
	this flag is used with msgrcv()

	Purpose 

		* Allows the message to be truncated if the message text is longer than msgsz		     * Prevents the receive operation from failing due to size mismatch 

	Without MSG_NOERROR

		msgrcv(id, &msg, msgsz, type, 0);

		if message size > msgsz 

			call fails 
			errno = E2BIG

 	With MSG_NOERROR

		msgrcv(id, &msg, msgsz, type, MSG_NOERROR);

			Message text is truncted 
			Extra bytes are discarded 
			Call succeeds 

	Example : 

		Situation 

			Message in queue = "HELLO WORLD" 
			Receiver buffer size = 5 bytes
		
		Without MSG_NOERROR 

			msgrcv(id, &msg, 5, 1, 0);
	
				* message size > buffer size 
				* Receive fails 
				* errno = E2BIG 

		With MSG_NOERROR

			msgrcv(id, &msg, 5, 1, MSG_NOERROR);
		
				* message is truncated 
				* Extra bytes are discarded	
				* Receive succeeds 

				Received data

					HELLO

		NOERROR = No error, just cut the message


































		



















	 
